  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY NIGHT THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 259 PM EDT Thu Aug 6 2026\n\nIsolated to scattered showers and storms will remain possible Friday \nnight into Saturday as a somewhat deeper shortwave trough develops \nsoutheast over the region. By Saturday afternoon and evening, the \nhighest coverage should be across the eastern half of KY as the mid-\nlevel trough axis moves overhead and sfc high pressure builds \nsoutheast over the Midwest. \n\nWe then transition to a slightly more deamplified upper level flow \npattern, with a weakening of the western CONUS ridge. We see a more \nactive WNW flow pattern, with the bulk of convection staying to our \nnorth. This should result in mostly dry weather Sunday into early \nnext week. Unfortunately, this respite looks to be short-lived. We \ncould get right back into an active NW flow pattern by Tuesday night \nor Wednesday, with multiple waves of convection possible through mid \nto late next week.",
